/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj127 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(  Exalted, Heroic.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 10 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920174806-03'00')/NM(bb138ce29a0f43518600d4a0c15c9228)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">  Exalted, Heroic.</span></p></body>)/Rect[258.547 267.566 352.043 289.576]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj128 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(Itês events were caused by the vehement refusal of the world on adopting the çSymmetry454é systemês main calendar, ultimately leading to itês adoption anyways. Existing in the Post Fifth Globe War timeline, it belongs to the now to a soldier of extinct co\untry named Perforides, serving the perforidian army division called the çCrashimesé, Wilhelm A. SoÎnder. The skull is carved with writings and symbols of old perforidian dialect around its skull cap, speculated to be chants related to its anomalous prope\rty. It is activated when an individual establishes physical contact with the object for a period longer than 10 seconds, in which they start showing symptoms such as nausea, dizziness, weakness, sleepiness and audiovisual hallucinations, gradually increa\sing in intensity the more time passes. At the end of the 10 seconds, the individual, in an unknown manner, is teleported to what can be described as a recreation of the events of the last battle of the war, in a limited space, confined to the Great Squar\e, completely destroyed at the time and littered with battle casualties from every party.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Arial 10 Tf)/DS(font: Arial,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920175205-03'00')/NM(d7acb930cdb148c288da8a71ac95f1c3)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:justify">It&#8217;s events were caused by the vehement refusal of the world on adopting the &#8220;Symmetry454&#8221; system&#8217;s main calendar, ultimately leading to it&#821\7;s adoption anyways. Existing in the Post Fifth Globe War timeline, it belongs to the now to a soldier of extinct country named Perforides, serving the perforidian army division called the &#8220;Crashimes&#8221;, Wilhelm A. So&#235;nder. The skull is ca\rved with writings and symbols of old perforidian dialect around its skull cap, speculated to be chants related to its anomalous property. It is activated when an individual establishes physical contact with the object for a period longer than 10 seconds,\ in which they start showing symptoms such as nausea, dizziness, weakness, sleepiness and audiovisual hallucinations, gradually increasing in intensity the more time passes. At the end of the 10 seconds, the individual, in an unknown manner, is teleported\ to what can be described as a recreation of the events of the last battle of the war, in a limited space, confined to the Great Square, completely destroyed at the time and littered with battle casualties from every party.</span></p></body>)/Rect[45.3301 40.864 571.312 206.874]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj129 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(   Dif)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240915200225-03'00')/NM(1136aaeffc294a48afa27816b1ee9af3)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1